#: processes/sdlc/sme-test-data-review.bpmn:19
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "SME review of fixed test data for clinical or scientific decision support and indicator definitions — bean `folio-assistant-vljz`, companion `folio-assistant-vm6m`, proposal `docs/proposals/qa-reports-branch-and-test-process-2026-10-01.md` §3.2. TWO UNITS OF REVIEW (`SmeCaseVerdictKind`, `$schema: \"sme-case-verdict/1.0.0\"` in `schemas/test-data.ts`): - `decision-support`: the unit of review is a **worked case** (`case`: input state, `decisionLogicRef`, `systemOutput`, optional `expectedGuidance`). - `indicator-definition`: the unit of review is a **cohort plus an expected value** (`cohort`: `indicatorRef`, `populationSize`, `inputs`, `expectedValue`, `computedValue`, optional `period`, `numerator`, `denominator`). JUDGEMENT-ONLY SME LANE. `Lane_SME` binds `clinical-sme`, which is declared `judgementOnly: true` in `scenarios/roles.json`. `Task_SmeJudge` carries no skill reference because no mechanical procedure yields the clinical or scientific answer — that is the whole reason a person is in the lane. ATTRIBUTABLE REVIEWER AND DATE. `Task_RecordCaseVerdict` writes the `sme-case-verdict/1.0.0` node with the SME's attributable human identity (`reviewer: { kind: \"human\", provider, handle, role }`) and ISO-8601 review date (`reviewedAt`), because an audited review without an attributable reviewer and date is not audited."
msgstr ""

